### Summary of Changes

#### 1. UI Quoting Wrapper Removal (`SessionSummaryDisplay.tsx`)
* **Issue**: The printed resume message was wrapped in unnecessary double quotes on Windows/PowerShell, preventing standard copy-pasting of the session IDs.
* **Resolution**: Removed the conditional `isWindows()` double-quote wrapping logic inside [SessionSummaryDisplay.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_26861/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/components/SessionSummaryDisplay.tsx), which now correctly yields the unquoted escaped session ID directly.
* **Tests**: Adjusted [SessionSummaryDisplay.test.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_26861/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/components/SessionSummaryDisplay.test.tsx) to assert that on Windows with PowerShell, the standard UUID-formatted footer displays cleanly without redundant quotes.

#### 2. Quote-tolerant Session Resolution (`sessionUtils.ts`)
* **Issue**: Users resolving sessions with enclosing quotes around the session ID would fail to match files cleanly.
* **Resolution**: Updated the entry point of `resolveSession` inside [sessionUtils.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_26861/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/utils/sessionUtils.ts) to detect and strip matched enclosing single (`'`) or double (`"`) quotes from the input argument before resuming.
* **Tests**: Added modular test cases to [sessionUtils.test.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_26861/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/utils/sessionUtils.test.ts) verifying successful resolution of UUIDs wrapped in double quotes (e.g. `"<session-id>"`), single quotes (e.g. `'<session-id>'`), and with surrounding helper whitespaces.

